the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob01re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}], "id": 0}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1, "id": 12}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n1le02ob01re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Professor:</strong> In this class, we are going to cover actors and actions involved in the business process. First, you have to remember that all businesses have processes. There are people and steps involved in them, and there is also a system that we use to get things done. For example, there are production, billing, and human resources processes, among others. <br /><strong>Megan:</strong> What about the actors and actions? <br /><strong>Professor:</strong> Well, a business process is a sequence of activities. First, you collect data about different actors who are in charge of the departments in the company. Then, in each department, we have to structure the actions that produce a service or a product."}, {"time": "44000", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Megan:</strong> How do we sequence the actors and actions? <br /><strong>Professor:</strong> You create a business process. Think about a procedure that involves ordering, producing, and selling a product with a swim lane flowchart. Ok, let's start with the diagram! Please, draw it at the top of your pages. Place the actors above the lines, and under each of them, write down their actions. The actions are going to be the steps of the business process. Write each name in a rectangle. <br /><strong>Megan:</strong> Ok, I am going to start with the ordering department. First, a client takes an order. Then, we have the production department where the material is ordered; and then, we schedule the production to manufacture the product."}, {"time": "88000", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Professor:</strong> What else? <br /><strong>Megan:</strong> Well, below the sales department we write \"ship the product.\" The last part is under the accounting department, which has to bill the customer. <br /><strong>Professor:</strong> Excellent. Now, you need to create the connections in order to add structure to this process. Please, establish the connections between actions and actors using arrows. Use diamonds instead to show decision points. <br /><strong>Megan:</strong> Ok, I place the arrows under the rectangles, and with this, we have a swim lane flowchart.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n1le02ob01re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}